<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin-bottom: 5px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin-top: 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Classroom News</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> We Need Pictures for the Classroom Newsletter.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Clarify spoken instructions in collaborative tasks.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can recognize main ideas in collaborative group discussions about a newsletter (e.g., 'A newsletter can include various types of information, such as announcements, projects, and current events.').<br>Can follow and clarify spoken instructions for making a class newsletter (e.g., 'First, write; then, draw.').<br>Can identify specific spoken instructions about a school trip (e.g., 'place to visit, date, activities').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 15%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b><br>Students are engaged with the topic and prior knowledge is activated. New vocabulary and pronunciation are introduced and clarified.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows a simple real-life school newsletter or a large picture of one, along with various photos (e.g., school events, students drawing, a school trip). The teacher asks, "What is this? What do you see in these pictures? What do you think a newsletter is for?" Students listen and respond using simple words or gestures. This activates prior knowledge about school news and visual information.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary orally, modeling pronunciation clearly. The teacher says words like "newsletter," "pictures," "article," "event," "announcement." Students listen and repeat chorally. The teacher specifically models short and long vowel sounds in orally stated single-syllable words relevant to the theme, for example, /ɑ/ in 'art' (pointing to a picture with art) and /oʊ/ in 'show' (as in 'show me the picture').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms using concept checking questions (CCQs).</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a newsletter a long story or a short paper with news?" (Expected answer: A short paper with news.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do we need only words or also pictures for our newsletter?" (Expected answer: Also pictures.)</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Students are exposed to new language through authentic input. The focus is on listening for gist and specific information related to the scenario "Our Classroom News."</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input Material:</b> A short audio recording (or teacher-read dialogue) of a teacher and two students discussing plans for the classroom newsletter. The dialogue includes present simple questions, future tense, and past simple. </p>
            <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Teacher:</b> "Good morning, class! We're planning our classroom *newsletter*. What *topic* will we discuss?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student A:</b> "How about our *school trip*? *Yesterday*, we went to the Emberá Community."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Teacher:</b> "That's a great *event*! When did this happen? It was very *exciting*! We need *pictures* for the *article* about it. What else do we need?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student B:</b> "I will *write* the *article*. What will *you* do?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student A:</b> "I'll *collect* the *photos* for the *newsletter*."</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Identifying specific instructions and main ideas from spoken interaction about planning a newsletter, including details about a past event.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> The teacher asks, "What are the teacher and students talking about?" (Expected answer: A classroom newsletter.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen again and indicate true or false for statements (e.g., "They went on a school trip today." - False; "They need pictures for the newsletter." - True).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> The teacher writes names (Student A, Student B) on the board and asks, "Who will write the article? Who will collect the photos?" Students listen and match the task to the person.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Students practice listening for specific details, using target grammar and vocabulary. Accuracy is the main focus in controlled and semi-controlled activities.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening to identify present simple questions ('What else do we need?'), future tense in affirmative ('I will write the article.') and interrogative sentences ('What will you do?'), and past simple in affirmative ('Yesterday, we went on a field trip.') and interrogative sentences ('When did this happen?'). Vocabulary: newsletter, pictures, article, event, announcement, school trip, write, collect, show, editor, yesterday, exciting. Pronunciation: Emphasizing the main verb in future tense contractions (e.g., 'I'll **go**', 'I'll **write**'). Identifying short /ɑ/ in 'art' and long /oʊ/ in 'show'.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Listen and Fill):</b> The teacher plays the dialogue again, but this time provides a transcript with specific target vocabulary words (e.g., 'newsletter', 'pictures', 'article', 'yesterday', 'will write', 'will do') removed. Students listen and fill in the blanks. The teacher pauses to allow students to check.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled (Listen and Draw/Point):</b> The teacher gives a series of simple instructions related to planning the newsletter, using target vocabulary and grammar. For example: "Listen. First, draw a *camera*. Then, point to the *pictures* on the board." "Listen to the instruction: 'I'll *go* on a school trip.' What did I emphasize? Go. Listen to 'I'll *write* the article.' What is emphasized? Write." Students listen and follow the instructions. This also reinforces main verb emphasis.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Listen and Confirm):</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher plays short audio snippets (e.g., "Student X says: 'I will be responsible for the *layout* of the page.' Student Y asks: 'Can you *write* the *article* about our *school trip*?'"). After each snippet, students tell their partner what they heard and confirm (e.g., "Student X will do the layout. Student Y asked about writing an article."). This integrates sociolinguistic competence by listening for collaborative language.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Students use the target language in a realistic communicative task. Fluency, collaborative interaction, and communicative task completion are prioritized.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Group Discussion / Mini-Role Play.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students work in small groups (3-4 students) to plan specific sections of a classroom newsletter. Each group receives a task card with a different topic (e.g., "Our Last School Trip," "Upcoming Class Event," "Student Art Corner").</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group discusses their assigned topic for the newsletter. Students must listen to each other and clarify instructions and roles.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They decide: "What information do we need?" "What *pictures* do we need for this *article*?" "Who will *collect* the *photos*?" "Who will *write* the *headline*?" "What will *you* do?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students should use future tense to describe plans ("I will...") and present simple questions ("What else do we need?") and past simple to refer to prior events ("Yesterday, we went..."). They are encouraged to use phrases like "Can you repeat that?" or "What do you mean by 'layout'?" to clarify spoken instructions and responsibilities, demonstrating sociolinguistic competence in teamwork.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, listens to groups, and provides support, encouraging the use of target language and clarification strategies.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>Formative assessment measures students' comprehension and production. Students also engage in self-reflection.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the group discussion (Performance Stage).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher observes student interactions in groups, specifically noting their ability to listen for and clarify instructions for the newsletter planning.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Listening Focus):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can recognize main ideas in collaborative group discussions (e.g., 'They are talking about the school trip').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can follow and clarify spoken instructions for making a class newsletter (e.g., 'First, write; then, draw.' 'Who will take the pictures?').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can identify specific spoken instructions about a school trip (e.g., 'place to visit, date, activities').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Attempts to use target vocabulary (e.g., *newsletter*, *pictures*, *article*, *write*, *collect*).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Attempts to use target grammar (e.g., "What will you do?", "When did this happen?").</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can listen for specific words like 'pictures' and 'newsletter' in a discussion." (Yes / A Little / No)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can ask questions to understand instructions better." (Yes / A Little / No)</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b><br>Students reflect on their learning and the teacher evaluates the lesson's effectiveness, planning for future lessons.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b> Students consider the following questions, either individually or in a brief class discussion:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy or difficult about listening to the instructions today when we planned our newsletter?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I improve my listening for details in English discussions?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What listening strategies worked well in engaging the students and helping them understand spoken instructions? (e.g., visual cues, repetition, peer collaboration).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students actively attempt to clarify spoken instructions and specific details? Were the A2.1 vocabulary, grammar, and pronunciation points accessible and reinforced effectively?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to further support listening comprehension and active clarification skills? (e.g., more structured sentence frames for asking questions, slower speaking pace).</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Next Lesson:</b> "Today, we focused on listening to understand what we need and how to plan our classroom newsletter, especially for *pictures* and *articles*. Next time, we will *read* an example *newsletter* to see how all these parts, like headlines and photos, fit together. This will help us understand different types of *articles* and *announcements*."</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>